     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi. I am a new Stan user and started using it aiming to estimate (filter) the latent jumps a discrete-time jump-diffusion model (below). Unfortunately, using this code, I can&#39;t even filter out the most obvious jump. That is, I use a T=600 sample where, for a given tn, eps[tn], a normal(0,1), would have to be -15 if no jump had occurred. Well... using the code below, eps[tn] is indeed -15, and y[tn] is virtually zero. Any idea what I am doing wrong? <div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// # time steps</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// # truncation of jump sum</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real </span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real wz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real wy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real az</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real ay</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real bz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real cz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real cy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real dz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real dy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real ez</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real ey</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real delta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real hz1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real hy1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style