    [
     1,
     "I&#39;m not familiar with th emodel you&#39;re trying to estimate\r<br>and those are a lot of variables to take in.\r<br>\r<br>Have you tried estimating something simpler and working\r<br>up to something of this complexity?\r<br>\r<br>Was your intention to just do the forward sampling for y?\r<br>There aren&#39;t any other parameters in the model.\r<br>\r<br>Whatever the case, your model block won&#39;t work because you\r<br>declare a local variable and then use it before defining it:\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br> int nJ[T];\r<br>  eps ~ normal(0,1);\r<br>  nJ  ~ poisson(hy);\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "The sampling statement does not define a variable.  It assumes\r<br>the variable is already defined and uses it to increment the overall\r<br>log density for the posterior.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
